genic  human derived microglial cell lines  the variants are introduced in these  cell lines  and  we see certain type of interesting  things  like the sorel one  micro clear  like cell lines induce trim to  expression which enhance  the apoe expression pathway  now the alzheimer's disorder associated  with sore l1 and trem2 mutations  uh also  impaired the  microglial cell lines  alpha beta uptake in the api dependent  manner in vitro of course  the  cd33 temp2 and sorel one  are all types  one membrane components highly expressed  in the microglial cell lines  when we have to characterize the effects  of alzheimer's disorder associated  variants in the microglial cell line  we  integrated all these mutation into the  h9esc line  by crisper cas9 editing and by v here i  don't mean i  i mean the  scientists who have written the research  paper  now the methodology i have adopted to  study the data set they accomplished is  basically  first of all we have to convert  the tpm values to raw counts  so preparing the raw counts  by  batch filtering and other  and  doing a quantile normalization for them  after that we analyze  all the raw counts and do a pci analysis  for all the different samples and all  the different sets  under different condition we compare  all those  variants separately and together with  the wild type to get a better idea of  what's happening with all those  different variants  then we do a gene ontology and  cake enrichment pathway analysis  which determines the overall direction  and the pathways involved  in the regulation of those  gene samples  now  we derive the volcano plot to find  the  log to fold charge versus the  p adjusted  value plots and then we finally reach to  the conclusion of which type of genes  are being upregulated or down regulated  and furthermore results  now coming on to a pc analysis pipeline  so we have used the  turn for browser provided by our  omixlogic website  to  do all our work and  as shown in the  diagram in 